<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vajiralongkorn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1952</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rama X</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vajiralongkorn, also known as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> X, has been king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> since 2016, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhumibol-adulyadej">Bhumibol Adulyadej</a>. Crowned in 2019, he has taken personal control of the Crown Property Bureau's assets and of some army units. Protests in 2020 called for reform of the monarchy, which remains protected by strict lèse-majesté laws.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vajiralongkorn.jpg" alt="Vajiralongkorn" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Public Relations Department (กรมประชาสัมพันธ์) · CC BY 3.0 th · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Rama_X_official_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
